// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 1, part (a) (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P8): a global text aliased into a global
// record's text field. Before the fix, the select-LHS store rule (Task 8's
// own window-var protection) disqualified only the FIELD NAME on a
// non-fresh store, never the record's own base -- `cl_free_globals` still
// recursed into `p8GRec`'s fields, freeing `body` (== `p8Gt`'s handle,
// after the store), then separately froze `p8Gt` itself: SIGSEGV. The fix
// adds `lowEscapeHandoff(selectX(lhs))` alongside the existing field-name
// disqualification, so a bare `base.field` store's BASE identifier
// (`p8GRec`) is disqualified too -- `cl_free_globals` skips it entirely,
// never recursing into its fields at all. Expected strict-mode leak count:
// 4 (see ../p8_rec_field.leaks) -- `p8Gt`'s "keep" text (struct box + data
// handle, 2 blocks; disqualified by the existing bare-ident-RHS-of-
// assignment handoff rule, shared with `p8GRec.body` after the store, so
// counted once) plus `p8ProbeNote`'s own default `body = "hi"` handle (2
// blocks), orphaned the instant the store overwrites the field without
// freeing the old value first -- same orphan-on-overwrite class as P2's
// `p2G2`, independent of this fix.

record p8ProbeNote {
    body: text = "hi"
}

var p8Gt: text = "keep"
var p8GRec: p8ProbeNote

func runP8RecField() {
    p8GRec.body = p8Gt
    alert("p8 done")
}
